==============================================================================
  HARNESS SELF-TEST — can this harness fail? (no database, no server)
==============================================================================

── A. free-to-promise arithmetic ───────────────────────────────
  [PASS] 4 on hand, 0 reserved -> 4 free
  [PASS] 10 on hand, 6 reserved -> 4 free
  [PASS] 6 on hand, 6 reserved -> 0 free
  [PASS] over-reserved lot reports NEGATIVE free, not a clamped 0

── B. VALID synthetic states — the detector must stay silent ───
  [PASS] consuming exactly the free stock is NOT an oversell
  [PASS]   and it reports the 4 units gained
  [PASS] taking less than was free is NOT an oversell
  [PASS] taking nothing when nothing is free is NOT an oversell
  [PASS] a net RELEASE is NOT an oversell
  [PASS]   and it reports a negative gain
  [PASS]   and overage is 0 when nothing was oversold

── C. INVALID synthetic states — the detector MUST fire ────────
  [PASS] 6 units taken from 4 free IS an oversell
  [PASS]   and the overage is reported as 2 units
  [PASS]   and the gain is reported as 6 units
  [PASS] exceeding free stock by a single unit IS an oversell
  [PASS]   overage 1
  [PASS] reserving against an empty shelf IS an oversell
  [PASS] a lot already over-reserved IS an oversell even with no new gain

── D. The original defect must be impossible to reintroduce ────
  [PASS] an undefined `free` raises instead of silently comparing false
  [PASS] an undefined reservedAfter raises
  [PASS] NaN raises — it compares false in every direction, exactly like undefined
  [PASS] an undefined balance raises in freeUnits too
  [PASS] an unguarded comparison against undefined answers false BOTH ways (why the guard exists)

── E. the runner must not accept an untrustworthy suite ────────
  [PASS] a suite that ran and asserted is accepted
  [PASS] a suite that reports failures and exits 1 is flagged once
  [PASS]   and the reason is its exit code
  [PASS] A. a non-zero exit is rejected
  [PASS] B. a suite that printed no summary is rejected
  [PASS]   and BOTH its exit code and its silence are reported
  [PASS]   a suite that exits 0 but printed no summary is STILL rejected
  [PASS] C. a suite reporting zero assertions is rejected
  [PASS]   a suite explicitly declared non-asserting is accepted
  [PASS]   the exemption applies only to the declared suite
  [PASS] D. a suite reporting failures but exiting 0 is rejected

==============================================================================
  REQUEST-KEY LIFECYCLE (client, no browser, no database)
==============================================================================
  [PASS] a holder mints nothing until an attempt is made
  [PASS] the first attempt mints a v4 UUID
  [PASS] asking again during the same attempt returns the SAME key
  [PASS] a 5xx leaves the operation unresolved and keeps the key
  [PASS] the retry after a 5xx carries the same key
  [PASS] a dropped connection (no status reported) also keeps the key
  [PASS] a 2xx retires the key
  [PASS] a genuinely new partial pack gets a DIFFERENT key
  [PASS] a 4xx refusal also retires the key
  [PASS] the corrected submit is a new operation, not a replay
  [PASS] separate holders never collide
  [PASS] 2000 generated keys are all distinct
  [PASS] the server validator accepts a client-generated key
  [PASS] a caller that sends no key gets a server-generated one, flagged as such
  [PASS] the validator still refuses a key outside the charset
  [PASS] the validator still refuses an unbounded key

==============================================================================
  REQUEST-KEY RETRY CLASSIFICATION
==============================================================================
  [PASS] 408 KEEPS the key — Request Timeout — abandoned in flight; the work may have finished anyway
  [PASS] 425 KEEPS the key — Too Early — decided below the application
  [PASS] 429 KEEPS the key — Too Many Requests — a 'try again', not a 'this did not happen'
  [PASS] 500 KEEPS the key — Internal Server Error
  [PASS] 502 KEEPS the key — Bad Gateway — a proxy answered, not the application
  [PASS] 503 KEEPS the key — Service Unavailable
  [PASS] 504 KEEPS the key — Gateway Timeout — the pack may have committed after the proxy gave up
  [PASS] 301 KEEPS the key — a redirect decides nothing about the operation
  [PASS] 599 KEEPS the key — an unknown status is treated as ambiguous, not as a decision
  [PASS] 0 KEEPS the key — no status at all
  [PASS] 200 RETIRES the key — packed
  [PASS] 201 RETIRES the key — packed
  [PASS] 204 RETIRES the key — packed
  [PASS] 400 RETIRES the key — validation refusal — nothing was written
  [PASS] 401 RETIRES the key — not authenticated — nothing was written
  [PASS] 403 RETIRES the key — not authorized — nothing was written
  [PASS] 404 RETIRES the key — no such batch — nothing was written
  [PASS] 409 RETIRES the key — status gate or insufficient stock — the transaction rolled back
  [PASS] 422 RETIRES the key — idempotency-key mismatch — the request was never executed
  [PASS] a 504 then a 429 then a 500 still leaves ONE key for the retry
  [PASS] and only the eventual success retires it

